From 2158ff0b7f5f6142d3fac10d719e4305fd76c044 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 18:24:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 30/30] NEXUS shared shader cache: portable shader data in a
 folder shared by NEXUS users

A session or shader preparation can name "shaderDir": EdenPath::ShaderDir then points there,
and it holds only what is the same on any GPU - the shader cache v2 log (guest programs,
pipeline keys, used lists; appends under its own file lock, records hashed, torn tails
skipped) and the precache files. What belongs to this user's GPU and driver stays in the
user's own cache folder (Common::FS::DeviceShaderDir): driver blobs, the Vulkan pipeline cache,
the static pipeline cache, the boot marker, and the precache's .done marker and progress (the
driver keeps its cache per Windows user, so another user's "done" says nothing about this
one's). Preparing the same game's shaders is serialised by a lock next to the precache file;
a second NEXUS waits and then finds the file current. Without "shaderDir" nothing changes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01X7yw1ZJY9GYi2KYHfiXxvY
